      "title": "Baroque Era Overview (1600–1750)",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** music-periods | **Difficulty:** 3/10 | **Time:** ~12 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Baroque: birth of opera, oratorio, concerto, and tonality as we know it. Bach, Handel, Vivaldi, Corelli dominate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "features",
      "title": "Features",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Basso continuo, terraced dynamics, doctrine of affections (specific emotions per movement). Equal temperament enabled all-key composition."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "forms",
      "title": "Forms",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Fugue, concerto grosso, suite, opera seria. Vivaldi's *Four Seasons*; Handel's *Messiah*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trad-link",
      "title": "Trad link",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Baroque dance rhythms feed into European folk dance; ornamentation practice influences traditional gracing."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
